<!--
HOW TO USE THIS TEMPLATE

Copy this file to:

  .claude/rules/critical.md

Claude Code loads Markdown files under .claude/rules/ recursively. No CLAUDE.md import is required.

Keep this file short. Use it only for invariants that are dangerous to forget:
- production and test data boundaries
- architectural rules that must hold across every caller
- known footguns
- model or tool routing rules
- the minimum verification required before reporting completion

Delete the placeholders below and replace them with project-specific directives. Prefer:

  NEVER do X because Y.
  ALWAYS do Z before W because Q.

Rules with a reason survive handoffs better than unexplained commands.
